    "inspection": "Exact current 20 EC project entries cover IRO, outgoing POL and outgoing IP. Their first-year completion, 40 EC year-two and methods requirements are route-specific. The older NIP faculty flyer puts economics in year one and Global History in year two, which conflicts with the current chart and formal appendix. The indexed current English regulations name the new NIP and refer mandatory sequence and assessment to the prospectus. Direct fetches of guessed Dutch PDF addresses returned access blocks, so those probes establish no document contents."
  },
  "findings": [
    "The three nominal year requests for the NIP study product return byte-identical copies of the exact current catalogue. Its only populated year group is the 60 EC first year. The separate IRO and outgoing track records cannot establish eligibility for NIP.",
    "The current programme overview confirms later-year multivariate analysis, qualitative methods, economics and rational choice, political philosophy, political psychology, and proposal, analysis and presentation work. It describes specialist seminars, a 30 EC elective space and an individual supervised thesis. The chart accounts for all 180 EC; exact later-year NIP course entries, restricted-choice offerings and seminar and thesis progression and assessment remain unconfirmed.",
    "The current regulations confirm the 180 EC degree, first-year registration and general degree outcomes. Appendix 1 gives the 60 EC exact NIP first year only. Articles 4.2 and 4.3 place compulsory sequencing and assessment methods in the prospectus."
  ],
  "unresolved": "Leiden’s programme chart accounts for all 180 EC. The course catalogue and regulations annex confirm the first-year requirements. The detailed second- and third-year course records, including seminar and thesis entry requirements, still need confirmation for this route.",
